NNAAMMEE
     clri - clear i-node

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     /eettcc/ccllrrii _f_i_l_e_s_y_s_t_e_m _i_n_u_m_b_e_r ...

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ccllrrii zeroes each i-node named by an _i_n_u_m_b_e_r argument on
     _f_i_l_e_s_y_s_t_e_m. _f_i_l_e_s_y_s_t_e_m should be the raw (character-special)
     device holding the file system, e.g.  /ddeevv/rrhhdd00. ccllrrii reads
     the superblock of _f_i_l_e_s_y_s_t_e_m to locate the i-node list,
     then, for each _i_n_u_m_b_e_r, reads the disk block containing that
     i-node, zeroes the i-node's entry in the in-memory copy of
     the block, and writes the block back.

     The i-node is identified purely by number; no check is made
     that it is of any particular type or that it is otherwise a
     sensible thing to clear.

