DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
     ccllrrii prints a diagnostic and exits 1 if _f_i_l_e_s_y_s_t_e_m cannot be
     opened, its superblock cannot be read, an _i_n_u_m_b_e_r is out of
     range for the file system, or a read or write error occurs.

NNOOTTEESS
     ccllrrii operates directly on the raw device and does not go
     through the file system; run it only on an unmounted file
     system, since any in-memory copy of the affected i-node will
     otherwise overwrite this change when it is later written
     back to disk.  If the i-node cleared belongs to the root
     file system, reboot immediately afterward.
